  "name": "audec",
  "description": "audec is a technical real-time audio analysis suite implemented in Rust, optimized for high-density signal visualization rather than aesthetic entertainment. The architecture utilizes PortAudio for multi-backend input capture and SDL2 for software-driven rendering of oscilloscope, spectrogram, and vectorscope views. It employs FFT-based spectral decomposition with configurable windowing and zero-crossing detection to provide precise temporal and frequency-domain insights into live audio streams.",
